      <h2 id="doctor">When to see a doctor</h2>

      <ul>
        <li>Any fracture from a fall at standing height or less, or new back pain with loss of height, which can be a spinal fracture.</li>
        <li>A T-score at or below -2.5, or a FRAX result above the threshold your doctor uses.</li>
        <li>Osteopenia at a young age, before menopause or in a man under 50, which needs a search for a cause such as thyroid, parathyroid, steroid use or coeliac disease.</li>
        <li>Long-term steroid tablets, which accelerate bone loss and often justify treatment earlier.</li>
      </ul>

